  "worked_solution": "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=\u2207\\times F=|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x} & \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y} & \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x} & \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y} & \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202z} \\\\ {x}^{2} & xz & {z}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}({z}^{2})-\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202z}(xz)]i-[\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}({z}^{2})-\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202z}({x}^{2})]j+[\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(xz)-\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}({x}^{2})]k \\\\  & =(0-x)i-(0-0)j+(z-0)k \\\\  & =-x\\,i+z\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{curl}\\,F$ at the point $(-2,-3,1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\text{curl}\\,F)(-2,-3,1) & =-(-2)\\,i+(1)\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i+\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
